# IDS React component naming (codegen)

When generating IDS React components (`lib/react/ids/<slug>/`, lib-generated Storybook):

- **Public JSX names, CSS classes, and `data-ids` are `Ids` + PascalCase anatomy name.**
  Root is `IdsAppShell`, not `AppShellRoot`. A slot is `IdsAppShellMastheadSlot`, not `AppShell.MastheadSlot`.
- **Do not use dotted compound selection as the public API** (`AppShell.MastheadSlot`, `Masthead.BrandSlot`). Export each slot as its own `Ids…` identifier and use those names in stories, docs, and examples.
- Keep `displayName` equal to the `Ids…` export (e.g. `IdsAppShellMastheadSlot`).
- Selectors: `className={styles["IdsAppShellMastheadSlot"]}` and `data-ids="IdsAppShellMastheadSlot"` — same string, no kebab-case, no Base UI `data-slot`.

```tsx
// BAD — dotted compound as the selection
<AppShell>
  <AppShell.MastheadSlot />
  <AppShell.BodyRow />
</AppShell>

// GOOD — Ids camelCase identifiers
<IdsAppShell>
  <IdsAppShellMastheadSlot />
  <IdsAppShellBodyRow />
</IdsAppShell>
```
